PNG XL (.pxl) — Combined License Notice
=======================================

The PXL project (libpxl and pxltool) is a thin codec that combines two
upstream libraries and a filtering technique from a third project. It adds
no proprietary terms of its own; it is distributed under the combination of
the licenses below, all of which are permissive.

  * PNG interop uses libpng          -> PNG Reference Library License v2
  * Compression uses Zstandard       -> BSD License (Meta Platforms, Inc.)
  * The reversible pixel filters are ported from Zpng
                                     -> BSD 3-clause (Christopher A. Taylor)

You must retain all three notices below when redistributing PXL.

Exception: ffmpeg/
------------------

The files under ffmpeg/ are not part of libpxl or pxltool. They are FFmpeg
source files -- meant to be copied into an FFmpeg tree and built there -- and
so they carry FFmpeg's own license, the GNU Lesser General Public License
version 2.1 or later, as stated in each file's header. Building FFmpeg with
--enable-libpxl does not change FFmpeg's license, because the permissive terms
above are LGPL-compatible.


